WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.520
Thinking mode asks a model to produce or use a longer reasoning

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.361
process before the final answer.

00:00:06.361 --> 00:00:08.571
That can help some language problems,

00:00:08.571 --> 00:00:12.254
but perception-heavy tasks first require accurate grounding in the pixels.

00:00:12.254 --> 00:00:17.042
More reasoning cannot recover text or objects the visual stage failed to capture.

00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:22.566
The referenced benchmark found that thinking mode could hurt some vision tasks through added latency,

00:00:22.566 --> 00:00:26.249
instability, or language reasoning that drifted away from visible evidence.

00:00:26.249 --> 00:00:31.037
Treat that as a testable observation, not a permanent rule for every model.

00:00:31.037 --> 00:00:35.088
For direct OCR, object listing, simple description, or routine event classification,

00:00:35.088 --> 00:00:38.771
start with thinking disabled when the model supports that option.

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:41.717
This can reduce output length and improve throughput.

00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:45.400
Compare accuracy and completion rather than assuming shorter is better.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.452
Reasoning may help after perception for charts, diagrams, multi-step visual questions,

00:00:49.452 --> 00:00:51.293
or combining several extracted facts.

00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:54.976
A useful workflow separates the steps: first report visible evidence,

00:00:54.976 --> 00:00:57.186
then reason from the reported evidence.

00:00:57.186 --> 00:01:01.605
Prompts should ask the model to state uncertainty and avoid unsupported claims.

00:01:01.605 --> 00:01:05.656
Review whether the explanation cites visible labels, positions, values, or objects.

00:01:05.656 --> 00:01:07.866
Fluent internal reasoning is not verification.

00:01:07.866 --> 00:01:11.181
Benchmark both modes with the same images and scoring.

00:01:11.181 --> 00:01:14.496
Measure grounding accuracy, latency, completion, consistency, and resource use.

00:01:14.496 --> 00:01:20.020
Enable thinking only when it produces a repeatable benefit for the actual task and hardware.
